1036:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c **** 
1037:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c **** /**
1038:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @ingroup tcp_raw
1039:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Connects to another host. The function given as the "connected"
1040:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * argument will be called when the connection has been established.
1041:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *  Sets up the pcb to connect to the remote host and sends the
1042:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * initial SYN segment which opens the connection. 
1043:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *
1044:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * The tcp_connect() function returns immediately; it does not wait for
1045:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * the connection to be properly setup. Instead, it will call the
1046:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * function specified as the fourth argument (the "connected" argument)
1047:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * when the connection is established. If the connection could not be
1048:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * properly established, either because the other host refused the
1049:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * connection or because the other host didn't answer, the "err"
1050:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * callback function of this pcb (registered with tcp_err, see below)
1051:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * will be called.
1052:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *
1053:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * The tcp_connect() function can return ERR_MEM if no memory is
1054:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * available for enqueueing the SYN segment. If the SYN indeed was
1055:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * enqueued successfully, the tcp_connect() function returns ERR_OK.
1056:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *
1057:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @param pcb the tcp_pcb used to establish the connection
1058:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @param ipaddr the remote ip address to connect to
1059:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @param port the remote tcp port to connect to
1060:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @param connected callback function to call when connected (on error,
1061:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****                     the err calback will be called)
1062:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @return ERR_VAL if invalid arguments are given
1063:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *         ERR_OK if connect request has been sent
1064:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *         other err_t values if connect request couldn't be sent
1065:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  */
